Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; 18 - Windows Update no longer installs drivers by itself.
; Why: after you install a graphics driver yourself, Windows Update can quietly replace it
; with an older or generic one. This keeps the driver you chose.
; Two settings: "never search Windows Update for drivers" and the policy "do not include
; drivers with Windows quality updates". Security updates still install as before.
; Afterwards you update drivers yourself (menu D in this tool, or the website of the maker).
; Windows Update may show "Some settings are managed by your organization": that is the policy.
; Undo: menu 7, then 18.
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\DriverSearching]
"SearchOrderConfig"=dword:00000000

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsUpdate]
"ExcludeWUDriversInQualityUpdate"=dword:00000001
